# Root .dockerignore.
#
# infra/gateway builds with the REPO ROOT as its context (it shares the token
# package with signaling/ via a `replace` directive, and copies client/dist).
# Without this file that context is the entire tree — including capture/, which
# is a Chromium embedder, and .claude/worktrees/, which holds full checkouts of
# this repo. Sending those to the daemon turns a two-second build into a very
# long one and can exhaust disk.
#
# Deny-list rather than allow-list: a new top-level directory should build, not
# silently vanish from the context.

# Full checkouts of this repo. See CLAUDE.md — anything walking the tree has to
# exclude these or it sees every file N+1 times.
.claude/

.git/
.github/

# The Chromium embedder. Large, and built by a separate out-of-tree lane.
capture/
patches/
build/

# Per-arch native binaries and build output; the image builds its own.
**/node_modules/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.log

# Docs, tests, and measurement artefacts: none are inputs to a service image.
docs/
harness/
tests/
verification/
conformance/
newtab-probe-out/

# Other services' build contexts.
infra/controllers/
infra/turn-issuer/
infra/observability/
infra/snapshots/
